{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_understanding_scope_decisions", "label": "Scope decisions (\u00a70)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Independent conversion rather than cleanup of SAP's assistant output; two first-class modes; Corpus A is the output-shape reference and Corpus B only a NEO-input data point; .xsjob/.xshttpdest/privileges/.xsaccess and .hdbtable are out entirely."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_developer_hours_saved", "label": "The objective function is developer hours saved", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every API is hand-tested afterwards regardless, which inverts the usual trade-off: converting 70% mechanically and flagging the other 30% loudly beats converting 95% and hiding where it guessed, because a wrong-but-confident output costs more to find than an honest gap."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_migration_kb", "label": "migration-kb (from-scratch knowledge base)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces SAP's HANA Application Migration Assistant rather than assisting it, on the grounds that its bulk mechanical conversion is exactly the unreliable part."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_cleanup_kb", "label": "cleanup-kb (clean up the assistant's output)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rejected as the tool's workflow because it depends on a GUI wizard in BAS that cannot be scripted into folder-in/folder-out; its 25-item checklist is still reused as the validation pass, and its intake model was never validated against real assistant output."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_never_invent_a_rule", "label": "Never invent a rule not demonstrated by a real file", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both the NEO source and the CF result are present, so always diff them directly; never infer the NEO source from the migrated output. Paired with: if fixing something requires understanding what the business logic is doing, that is a red flag \u2014 flag it, don't guess."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_corpus_a", "label": "Corpus A (TECK) \u2014 the output-shape reference", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "848 NEO files hand-migrated; the only reference for what this tool's output should look like."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_corpus_b", "label": "Corpus B (ICBC) \u2014 NEO input shape only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Migrated with SAP's assistant plus Claude Code cleanup, so its CF side shows what the assistant emits, not what this tool should emit \u2014 which also resolves the 584 .hdbview that exist in CF and nowhere in NEO."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_calc_view_pipeline", "label": "The calc-view 1:1:1:1 pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "454 .calculationview \u2192 454 .hdbcalculationview + 454 TABLE_FUNCTION_*.hdbfunction + 454 db/cds proxies. Not approximately \u2014 exactly. ~53% of all NEO files in Corpus A and the single biggest, safest win available."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_tables_not_from_neo", "label": "Tables do not come from NEO", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Corpus A has 6 .hdbtable in NEO and 58 in CF; Corpus B has zero and 721. Table DDL is produced by a separate tool from the live HANA catalog, so the tool should detect the gap and say so rather than generate them."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_folder_mapping", "label": "The verified NEO \u2192 CF folder mapping", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "db/cds drops the <APP> wrapper, srv/lib/<SCHEMA>/<APP> keeps it, and the CF bucket name equals the real NEO top-level folder name \u2014 never relabelled into Env_Config/Inbound/Outbound."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_flattening_rule", "label": "The entity-name flattening rule", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every . and :: becomes _ and the whole string is uppercased \u2014 but the corpus shows the same view flattened two different ways in two modules, so it is not fully deterministic in the reference. The tool makes its own scheme authoritative and self-consistent."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_numeric_leading_rule", "label": "The numeric-leading identifier rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CDS/HDI reject identifiers starting with a digit, and the hand migration renamed the same NEO alias to different CF names in different modules. The tool uses a deterministic scheme and emits the before/after table \u2014 determinism is for the tool, the table is for the humans whose UI calls those names."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_checklist_final", "label": "The 24/25-item migration checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No checklist item was left correct in the assistant's raw output \u2014 every one required a manual edit or verification. The assistant's value is bulk file generation, not correctness of these details."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_7c_vs_14_boundary", "label": "The 7c-vs-14 request boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The two checklist items look contradictory but apply to different layers: entry functions take req directly, everything they fan out to takes primitives. The test is distance from the request, not the function's folder."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_graphify_survey", "label": "The graphify survey of the CF tree", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Blind to NEO \u2014 it recognised 5 of 848 files and would need an extension shim. On the CF side it produced 489 nodes and 1542 edges from 91 files and surfaced a validation layer neither knowledge base documents."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_cf_only_files", "label": "CF-only files with no NEO ancestor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ValidationUtil, Middleware, rate limiting and the rest were written by hand during the migration, not translated. The tool must not scaffold them; they matter because they are noise when diffing CF against NEO to derive a rule, and because they set the ceiling honestly \u2014 a perfect run still does not produce the finished CF app."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_no_ai_ceiling", "label": "The no-AI ceiling (~88% of in-scope files)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The deterministic band is not a fallback \u2014 it is the bulk of the work, and it is the part that is tedious and error-prone by hand."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_out_of_scope_artifacts", "label": "Out-of-scope artifact types", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "116 files inventoried but not converted, so nothing vanishes silently; scoping them out loudly is better than a half-answer."}, {"id": "docs_understanding_graphify_cache_incident", "label": "The graphify cache-write incident", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "extract(cache_root=...) wrote a graphify-out/cache/ directory into two reference codebases the KBs forbid modifying \u2014 concrete evidence for why the never-write-to-NEO guard lives in code rather than in a convention."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_understanding_scope_decisions", "target": "docs_understanding_out_of_scope_artifacts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/UNDERSTANDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_understanding_scope_decisions", "target": "docs_understanding_migration_kb", "relation": "references", "confi